{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NHznBaywd7YoqFysnHrm7R","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9","date":"2026-10-07T21:48:50+03:00","message":"(fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack (#423)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack\n\nThe run report and edit scheduled report forms now put their fields in\na Stack with gap={5}, and the form container sets the 16px padding.\nBefore, each field set its own spacing: fixed heights with\n30px bottom margins, an extra 50px margin and 32px top padding on the\noutput format select, and 16px padding on each parameter and the cron\neditor. That left uneven gaps between the fields.\n\nThe Report and Output format selects also lose their fixed 300px width,\nso every field in both forms is full width like the parameter inputs.\n\n* Keep the cron editor's floated fields inside its wrapper\n\nThe schedule fields float, so the editor's wrapper only had a height\nbecause the Stack around it is a grid. display: flow-root makes the\nwrapper contain them in any parent.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"feb0ba00e3382e0c55e4b3615648217d7d619198","date":"2026-10-01T22:20:05+03:00","message":"(chore) Remove unused stylesheet classes from the reports app","refs":"","body":"Delete 13 CSS Module classes in esm-reports-app that no component\nreferences. Each stylesheet is a CSS Module, so a class only applies\nwhen a file that imports that stylesheet uses it as styles.<name>, and\nnone of these are:\n\n- root.scss: welcome, explainer (plus the @carbon/type import, which\n  only welcome used)\n- components/reports.scss: emptyButton, breadcrumbsSlot\n- components/overlay.scss: closeButton, overlayContent (the desktop and\n  tablet breakpoint blocks contained only overlayContent)\n- components/run-report/run-report-form.scss: parameterElement,\n  cancelActionButton, tableIcon, rowCellEven, rowCellOdd\n- components/edit-scheduled-report/edit-scheduled-report-form.scss:\n  reportButton\n- components/simple-cron-editor/simple-cron-editor.scss: cronEditor\n\nrowCellEven, rowCellOdd and reportButton are still in use, but from\nother stylesheets: the overview tables use the copies in reports.scss,\nand the run report form uses the copy in run-report-form.scss. Only the\nunreferenced duplicates are removed.\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"9795d776cd61b56114d4da597e9b0be1abbe5ff5","date":"2025-06-03T13:37:50-04:00","message":"(fix) Fix the auto-update script and update to the latest version of core (#99)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"c77f2646e2177259acdfe86194e2a50fc389bf24","date":"2025-02-17T20:24:03+01:00","message":"(refactor) O3-1494: Restore functionality of the reports page (#61)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"druchniewicz","authorEmail":"51370022+druchniewicz@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"5e244cc84ea83c76e7d4a1127fdb5d1109fac82a","date":"2025-02-10T15:05:58+03:00","message":"(chore) Code quality and tooling improvements (#59)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Code quality and tooling improvements\n\nThis PR includes a number of changes to improve code quality and tooling. These changes include:\n\n- Adding ESLint plugins for testing (jest-dom, testing-library, playwright) and import rules for preventing duplicate imports.\n- Adding the react-hooks ESLint plugin for enforcing rules of hooks and exhaustive-deps for React hooks.\n- Resolving rules-of-hooks violations flagged by the react-hooks ESLint plugin.\n- Adapting the Prettier configuration to align with similar configurations in O3.\n- Adding emojis to steps in the GitHub Actions workflows.\n- Improving the `react-i18next` test mock to properly handle interpolated values in translation strings.\n- Annotating type-only imports with the `type` keyword.\n\n* Review feedback - reorganize imports","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"626b777d3894b352df757af94422b6f8a3852a19","date":"2025-02-06T12:31:06+01:00","message":"(feat) O3-1494: Add report admin dashboard (#45)","refs":"","body":"* O3-1494: Added Report Admin pages\n\n- Reports overview\n- Report schedules overview\n\n* O3-1494: Adjusted API calls to backend changes\n\n* O3-1494: Changes after code review\n\n* O3-1494: Changes after code review part2\n\n* O3-1494: Updated backend dependencies\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: druchniewicz <druchniewicz@soldevelo.com>","authorName":"pwargulak","authorEmail":"pwargulak@soldevelo.com"}],"totalCount":6}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15d591fa-b7e6-4fb8-8b9b-5684a1b58a32","uuid":"f82eaa86-a7b1-41a0-bcb3-ccf701f0ec3c","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:51:04.862Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9","date":"2026-10-07T21:48:50+03:00","message":"(fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack (#423)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack\n\nThe run report and edit scheduled report forms now put their fields in\na Stack with gap={5}, and the form container sets the 16px padding.\nBefore, each field set its own spacing: fixed heights with\n30px bottom margins, an extra 50px margin and 32px top padding on the\noutput format select, and 16px padding on each parameter and the cron\neditor. That left uneven gaps between the fields.\n\nThe Report and Output format selects also lose their fixed 300px width,\nso every field in both forms is full width like the parameter inputs.\n\n* Keep the cron editor's floated fields inside its wrapper\n\nThe schedule fields float, so the editor's wrapper only had a height\nbecause the Stack around it is a grid. display: flow-root makes the\nwrapper contain them in any parent.",